From a49e1d829a699b37b669309c6a6b709c542987b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:50:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(network): demote testbed peers that read block
 responses slowly

Priority fill ranks peers by measured throughput, so a peer that looks fast
but reads slowly could hold the first upload slot. Each block response now
starts a watchdog: if it is still running when a reader at a quarter of the
expected rate would have finished, the response gives up its upload slot and
the peer's rank is capped at the rate it actually read at. A normal response
later lifts the cap. Testbed-only, behind the testbed feature.
---
